WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.010
Fans have yet to catch a glimpse at Hulk in
any Avengers: Endgame footage, but promotional

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:09.620
materials have made their way online and made
it plain as day: Hulk is coming back.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:10.720
But how?

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.880
A new toy leak is spilling the details, revealing
something major about Hulk's arc in the film.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.339
Action figure photos that were recently leaked
show Hulk's ultimate form in action, with

00:00:20.339 --> 00:00:24.270
the newly-confident superhero sporting all
the brawn of the big green guy, with what

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:28.210
certainly looks like the intellect of Bruce
Banner, all wrapped up in one of the Avengers'

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.380
fancy new suits.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.960
But that's not the only leak of Hulk's new
form.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.700
Another photo of the packaging for a different
'Titan Heroes' Hulk action figure by Hasbro

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.620
shows Hulk suited up in the same silvery-white,
red, and black uniform that his fellow Avengers

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:46.310
sported in the latest Endgame trailer, which
many have theorized to be related to the bulky

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.960
Quantum suits last seen in Ant-Man and the
Wasp.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.200
Most importantly, the text accompanying the
drawing details the circumstances that will

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:57.580
lead to Banner becoming this all-new version
of the Hulk: "Bruce Banner masters his temper

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.120
to become the giant, super-strong hero, Hulk."

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.300
That's a little bit different from the way
we're used to Hulk doing things.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.580
"That's my secret, Cap — I'm always angry."

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.920
The idea that Banner has to master his temper
again to be able to go green in Endgame is

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.320
intriguing, building on the emotional trauma
and fear Hulk displayed after Thanos, well,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.260
Hulked out on him in Infinity War.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:26.140
So it makes sense that Endgame could feature
Banner getting a grip on his temper in order

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.391
to become not just the Hulk, but Professor
Hulk, an elevated version of the character

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.670
from Marvel Comics lore.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.580
If successfully fusing the brains of Bruce
with the might of Hulk is what it's going

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.840
to take to bring the big green guy back, maybe
that's why he hasn't been seen in any Endgame

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:40.840
footage yet.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.190
It'd be a pretty natural endgame for the character's
arc as well - after all, he's been getting

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:47.799
a lot better at talking things through over
the years.

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:49.830
"This is what friends do, they support each
other."

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.020
"You're Banner's friend."

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.340
"I'm not Banner's friend.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.340
I prefer you!"

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.340
"Banner's friend!"

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.740
"I don't even like Banner…"

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.300
If you're unfamiliar with this particular
twist on the character, we'll break things

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.120
down for you.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:03.460
Professor Hulk isn't a Hulk that completed
a doctorate degree.

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:08.170
Instead, he's a merged form of Bruce Banner,
the poor human scientist whose exposure to

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.920
gamma radiation split his personality; the
"Savage" Hulk, which is the green Hulk fans

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.000
are most familiar with; and the Gray Hulk,
the somewhat intelligent, original Hulk from

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:17.500
the comics.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.200
"Who are you?"

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.100
"They call me Mr. Fix-It."

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:31.500
Introduced in 1991's The Incredible Hulk #377,
Professor Hulk is his own entity - not a cut-and-dry

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.820
merger of the three different Hulk personalities,
but rather Bruce Banner's ideal self.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:40.540
He possesses Banner's intelligence, Savage
Hulk's super-strength, and Grey Hulk's cunning

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.950
- plus a more human face and an ability to
maintain power while keeping his cool.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:49.430
However, there's a catch - if Professor Hulk
becomes too angry, that inner peace of his

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:54.240
will be broken, leading him to turn back into
a Bruce Banner who is anything but mild-mannered.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.420
If Professor Hulk is something of a scientist
in Hulk's body, then his version of Bruce

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.870
is basically the Savage Hulk in human form.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.059
That catch is important to be aware of, and
the rest of the backstory seems to tie into

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.160
the information included in this toy leak.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.680
The only way Endgame could feature Professor
Hulk is if Banner takes the reins on his temper

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.400
and keeps his emotions in check.

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:17.400
If he can maintain the balance, he might just
become the most powerful version of himself

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.400
he could possibly be.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:23.040
Banner taking control of his anger in Endgame
would wrap up a three-movie arc for the character

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.720
that began with Thor: Ragnarok in 2017.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:31.040
According to Mark Ruffalo, Hulk's speech evolution
is a crucial element of the character's metamorphosis

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.529
from Ragnarok, and the first sign that Banner
and Hulk were starting to separate from one

00:03:35.529 --> 00:03:36.140
another.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.420
As the actor put it,

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:41.920
"Hulk speaking is the start to [a] separating
of these two individuals, these identities

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:45.260
in this split-identity person, and where that's
going to end up going."

00:03:45.669 --> 00:03:50.020
There are plenty of unanswered questions Avengers:
Endgame will hopefully address, not the least

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.800
of which is how and why Banner will Hulk out
once again.

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:57.960
But thanks to Ruffalo's comments, this purported
toy leak, and the sheer weight of fan expectations,

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.840
we're pretty confident it's going to happen.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.960
When he does show up, he'll likely be dramatically
different from how we've seen him before.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.700
Whatever ends up happening to the big green
dude, one thing seems undeniable: he's probably

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:12.200
going to be far more important in Endgame
than anyone realizes.

